1
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:03,478
Playing Games

2
00:00:03,478 --> 00:00:03,978
Oh, Daddy!

3
00:00:03,978 --> 00:00:06,272
We had such a good time at the aquarium.

4
00:00:06,272 --> 00:00:07,849
I saw a real shark.

5
00:00:07,849 --> 00:00:10,267
I could almost touch it.

6
00:00:10,267 --> 00:00:12,162
I'm so glad.

7
00:00:12,162 --> 00:00:12,662
Hi. Michelle,

8
00:00:12,662 --> 00:00:14,890
why don't you introduce everybody to Susan?

9
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:16,461
Hi, Susan.

10
00:00:16,461 --> 00:00:16,673
Hi.

11
00:00:16,673 --> 00:00:19,925
I'd like you to meet Audrey and her mother, Mrs. Cooper.

12
00:00:19,925 --> 00:00:20,418
Hello, Audrey.

13
00:00:20,418 --> 00:00:21,846
Nice to meet you, Mrs. Cooper.

14
00:00:21,846 --> 00:00:23,824
I'm Susan Stewart.

15
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:26,802
And this is Shirley and Nicole.

16
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:27,502
Hi, girls.

17
00:00:27,502 --> 00:00:28,552
Come on in.

18
00:00:28,552 --> 00:00:30,280
Come on in, Mrs. Cooper.

19
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,447
Come on in, everybody.

20
00:00:31,447 --> 00:00:33,098
The aquarium was so exciting.

21
00:00:33,098 --> 00:00:35,138
I had never been there before.

22
00:00:35,138 --> 00:00:36,760
The girls learned a great deal.

23
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:37,784
Frankly, so did I.

24
00:00:37,784 --> 00:00:39,290
Well, please sit down

25
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:41,692
and tell us all about it during lunch.

26
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:45,442
We prepared some tuna fish

27
00:00:45,442 --> 00:00:49,107
and cheese sandwiches for lunch.

28
00:00:49,107 --> 00:00:50,625
I love tuna fish.

29
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:51,532
Don't you, Audrey?

30
00:00:51,532 --> 00:00:54,936
I remember when I used to be a Girl Scout.

31
00:00:54,936 --> 00:00:57,311
My mother would take us everywhere, too.

32
00:00:57,311 --> 00:01:00,104
Susan, I understand you're in the toy business.

33
00:01:00,104 --> 00:01:00,923
Yes, I am.

34
00:01:00,923 --> 00:01:03,204
My company manufactures toys and games for children.

35
00:01:03,204 --> 00:01:05,737
Susan's vice-president in charge of new toys and games.

36
00:01:05,737 --> 00:01:07,515
And the marketing of new toys and games.

37
00:01:07,515 --> 00:01:09,364
Can we test a new game for you, Susan?

38
00:01:09,364 --> 00:01:10,234
That's an excellent idea, Michelle.

39
00:01:10,234 --> 00:01:10,931
I happen to have

40
00:01:10,931 --> 00:01:12,871
a game which I brought home to study.

41
00:01:12,871 --> 00:01:13,804
Let us try it!

42
00:01:13,804 --> 00:01:15,649
Do you want to play?

43
00:01:15,649 --> 00:01:17,856
Nicole? Shirley? Audrey?

44
00:01:17,856 --> 00:01:21,769
We tested it last week on twelve- to fifteen-year-olds,

45
00:01:21,769 --> 00:01:24,903
and they found it to be too easy--

46
00:01:24,903 --> 00:01:26,361
in other words ... boring.

47
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:29,339
We think it might be just right for ten- to twelve-year-olds.

48
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:30,625
That's us, Susan.

49
00:01:30,625 --> 00:01:33,501
First, you shuffle the deck

50
00:01:33,501 --> 00:01:38,273
and lay them face down.

51
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:41,251
Then you select the leader.

52
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:43,681
I'll be the leader.

53
00:01:43,681 --> 00:01:45,863
The leader takes the first ten cards

54
00:01:45,863 --> 00:01:49,487
and lays them face up on this stand.

55
00:01:49,487 --> 00:02:06,484
h-t-e-r-c-z-e-p-e-s.

56
00:02:06,484 --> 00:02:12,744
Everyone gets a turn, going counterclockwise,

57
00:02:12,744 --> 00:02:14,008
left to right.

58
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:18,486
You have thirty seconds to make a word,

59
00:02:18,486 --> 00:02:22,093
using as many letters as possible.

60
00:02:22,093 --> 00:02:25,085
You get one point for each letter,

61
00:02:25,085 --> 00:02:30,098
plus the person with the longest word gets ten extra points.

62
00:02:30,098 --> 00:02:33,001
The first one to get one hundred points wins.

63
00:02:33,001 --> 00:02:33,751
That's easy.

64
00:02:33,751 --> 00:02:37,187
OK, let's go around the table.

65
00:02:37,187 --> 00:02:38,187
You first, Audrey.

66
00:02:38,187 --> 00:02:39,932
Chest--c-h-e-s-t.

67
00:02:39,932 --> 00:02:40,232
Good.

68
00:02:40,232 --> 00:02:50,744
That's five points.

69
00:02:50,744 --> 00:02:53,662
Next, Nicole.

70
00:02:53,662 --> 00:02:58,678
Three--t-h-r-e-e.

71
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:00,618
OK.

72
00:03:00,618 --> 00:03:10,589
That's five points also.

73
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:14,167
It's your turn, Shirley.

74
00:03:14,167 --> 00:03:17,345
Creep--c-r-e-e-p.

75
00:03:17,345 --> 00:03:17,745
Creep.

76
00:03:17,745 --> 00:03:31,435
That's another five-letter word.

77
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:32,935
Five points.

78
00:03:32,935 --> 00:03:35,877
So far, you're all tied.

79
00:03:35,877 --> 00:03:38,805
Sheet--s-h-e-e-t.

80
00:03:38,805 --> 00:03:41,638
Sheet is a five-letter word.

81
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:42,906
Michelle, your turn.

82
00:03:42,906 --> 00:03:46,127
Cheese--c-h-e-e-s-e.

83
00:03:46,127 --> 00:03:46,327
Terrific!

84
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:50,028
Michelle wins with a six-letter word,

85
00:03:50,028 --> 00:03:53,372
plus she gets an additional ten points

86
00:03:53,372 --> 00:03:55,008
for a total of sixteen points.

87
00:03:55,008 --> 00:03:57,884
How are you enjoying the game so far?

88
00:03:57,884 --> 00:03:59,126
I think it's too easy.

89
00:03:59,126 --> 00:03:59,570
Too easy?

90
00:03:59,570 --> 00:03:59,793
Michelle!

91
00:03:59,793 --> 00:04:01,882
It's OK, Harry.

92
00:04:01,882 --> 00:04:04,193
Michelle is quite right.

93
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:07,971
She just said it's too easy.

94
00:04:07,971 --> 00:04:09,587
Well, I like the game.

95
00:04:09,587 --> 00:04:11,149
I enjoyed lunch, Susan.

96
00:04:11,149 --> 00:04:13,797
Thank you so much,

97
00:04:13,797 --> 00:04:16,105
but we have to get going

98
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:18,510
to meet the rest of the troop at two o'clock at the museum.

99
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:21,083
Oh, it was nice meeting all of you.

100
00:04:21,083 --> 00:04:22,295
I hope you have a wonderful time

101
00:04:22,295 --> 00:04:23,705
at the Museum of Natural History.

102
00:04:23,705 --> 00:04:24,410
Good-bye, everybody.

103
00:04:24,410 --> 00:04:26,178
Have a good time.

104
00:04:26,178 --> 00:04:26,748
Bye.

105
00:04:26,748 --> 00:04:29,445
See you in front of the museum at five o'clock.

106
00:04:29,445 --> 00:04:30,994
Oh, OK.

107
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:32,007
Thanks, Mr. Bennett.

108
00:04:32,007 --> 00:04:33,021
That'll be fine.

109
00:04:33,021 --> 00:04:36,950
And thanks again for the lunch and for the game.

110
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:38,470
Good-bye, Susan.

111
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:41,688
It's not a bad game.

112
00:04:41,688 --> 00:04:43,906
It's just ... slow.

113
00:04:43,906 --> 00:04:45,884
Just slow.

114
00:04:45,884 --> 00:04:48,862
You helped save our company a lot of money.

115
00:04:48,862 --> 00:04:57,796
Bye-bye.

116
00:04:57,796 --> 00:05:03,752
You are wonderful with kids.

117
00:05:03,752 --> 00:05:04,952
I am.

118
00:05:04,952 --> 00:05:07,952
Isn't there a conversation that we have to finish?
